ry and that is something that is  also at the moment being considered by  tc39 how to best extend it because it  doesn't come for free I mean with  upgrading is for example it's easier if  you just host a module in NPM and with  the standard library you really just  want to have the core functionality and  one kind of cosmetic thing that I would  like to see is at the moment javascript  has several namespace objects and these  are kind of poor-man's modules and they  exist because in the beginning they  wanted to group sets of functions but  javascript didn't have modules yet so  what you did was you just introduced the  namespace object instead it'd be nice if  they were actually built in modules and  this is what this could look like you'd  introduce a special protocol to have  this kind of identifier for for built-in  modules and it's import function max  from this module you would use it down  here and this is opposed to the current  way of doing things  we'll use the name space object math  and the advantage is that the language  becomes more modular and if he imports  something from a module the the invoking  that is quicker than doing finding a  property on on an object such as math  one functionality that I think should  definitely be added to the standard  library our helps for iterables and  ideally or it should be both synchronous  iterables and asynchronous intervals and  at the moment if you have an iterable  like up here this is a set if you want  to do anything with it such as filter it  you have to convert it into an array  before you can process it further and if  you had actually a helper that worked  directly with iterables you could do it  like down here you could apply filter  directly to the iterable and produce  another iterable and that would allow  nice on-demand pipelining of the whole  thing so that would be really great to  have Python is inspiring in that regard  they have a module it's called itertools  and they have a lot of tool funct